.TITLE "tmutil"

.DIV "DESCRIPTION"
Interacts with the Time Machine backup system on macOS. This command-line utility
allows users to control Time Machine backups, including starting/stopping backups,
listing snapshots, restoring items, and managing exclusions. It provides advanced
control over Time Machine operations.

.DIV "ALIAS"
**timemachineutil**

.DIV "TLDR"
**tmutil status**
Displays the current status of Time Machine, including if a backup is in progress.
> 

**tmutil startbackup**
Initiates a Time Machine backup immediately.
> 

**tmutil stopbackup**
Stops a currently running Time Machine backup.
> 

**tmutil latestbackup**
Prints the path to the latest completed Time Machine backup.
> 

**tmutil restore __/path/to/item__ __/destination__**
Restores an item from a Time Machine backup to a specified __/destination__.
> __/path/to/item__: The path to the item within the Time Machine backup. | __/destination__: The destination path for the restored item.

.DIV "SUMMARY"
`tmutil` offers powerful control over Time Machine. Be careful when using restore
commands to avoid overwriting newer data. Regular backups are crucial, and `tmutil`
can be integrated into scripts for automated backup management.

.DIV "SEE ALSO"
**mac:diskutil**

